I have implemented the `UserProfile` component in `app/UserProfile.tsx` adhering to the existing server component patterns.

**Changes made:**
-   Implemented `UserProfile` as an async Server Component.
-   Added a `User` interface for type safety.
-   Added data fetching from `http://localhost:3000/api/users/profile`.
-   Included a `try/catch` block to handle fetch failures (which occurred during the build as expected) and return fallback mock data, matching the pattern in `page.tsx`.
-   The component displays the user's name and email.

Verified the changes by running `npm run build`, which completed successfully using the fallback data.

```tsx
interface User {
  name: string;
  email: string;
}

async function getUser(): Promise<User> {
  try {
    const res = await fetch('http://localhost:3000/api/users/profile');
    if (!res.ok) {
      throw new Error('Failed to fetch user data');
    }
    return res.json();
  } catch (error) {
    // Return mock data for build time or when API is unavailable
    console.error(error);
    return {
      name: 'John Doe',
      email: 'john@example.com'
    };
  }
}

export default async function UserProfile() {
  const user = await getUser();

  return (
    <div>
      <h2>User Profile</h2>
      <div>Name: {user.name}</div>
      <div>Email: {user.email}</div>
    </div>
  );
}
```
